title: Presidential Election Candidates
subtitle: Should we field our own candidate?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1932 and month >= 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.presidential_election_campaigning_seen = 1;

Q.weimar_votes = Q.spd_votes + Q.ddp_votes + Q.z_votes;

Q.bourgeois_votes = Q.ddp_votes + Q.dbp_votes + Q.csrp_votes + Q.z_votes + Q.bvp_votes + Q.csvd_votes + Q.dvp_votes + Q.wp_votes + Q.cnblp_votes + Q.kvp_votes + Q.other_votes;
if (Q.dnvp_left >= 0) Q.bourgeois_votes = Q.bourgeois_votes + Q.dnvp_votes;

Q.antidem_votes = Q.kpd_votes + Q.dnf_votes + Q.nsdap_votes;
if (Q.dnvp_left < 0) Q.antidem_votes = Q.antidem_votes + Q.dnvp_votes;

if (!Q.hitler_deported) {
    Q.nsdap_candidate = "Hitler";
} else {
    Q.nsdap_candidate = "Göring";
}

if (Q.dnvp_left < 0) Q.dnvp_candidate = "Duesterberg";
Q.dnf_candidate = "Duesterberg";

Q.kpd_candidate = "Thälmann";
Q.sapd_candidate = "Thälmann";

Q.event_points = 0;
if (Q.nsdap_votes < 20) Q.event_points = Q.event_points + 1;
if (Q.pro_republic > 60) Q.event_points = Q.event_points + 1;
if (Q.weimar_votes > Q.antidem_votes) Q.event_points = Q.event_points + 1;
Q.spd_campaign = 0;
if (Q.event_points >= 2) {
    Q.spd_campaign = 1;
    if (Q.spd_left >= 3) {
        Q.spd_candidate = "Rosenfeld";
        Q.ddp_candidate = "Rosenfeld";
        Q.csrp_candidate = "Rosenfeld";
    } else {
        Q.spd_candidate = "Braun";
        Q.ddp_candidate = "Braun";
        Q.csrp_candidate = "Braun";
        if (Q.z_leader == "Joos" || Q.z_leader == "Kaiser") Q.z_candidate = "Braun";
    } 
}

Q.dvp_campaign = 0;

Q.second_reactionary_candidate = 0;
if (Q.hindenburg_run) {
    Q.reactionary_candidate = "Hindenburg";

    if (!Q.spd_campaign) {
        Q.spd_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        Q.ddp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        Q.csrp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    }
    if (Q.z_candidate != "Braun") Q.z_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.dbp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.bvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.csvd_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.cnblp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.wp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.kvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    if (Q.dnvp_left >= 0) Q.dnvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.other_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
} else {
    Q.reactionary_candidate = 0;

    if (Q.z_candidate != "Braun" && !Q.cvp_formed){
        if (Q.stegerwald_path) Q.adenauer_candidacy = 1;
        if (!Q.stegerwald_path && Q.chancellor != "Brüning" && Q.bourgeois_votes >= 40) Q.bruning_candidacy = 1;
        if (!Q.stegerwald_path && Q.adenauer_candidacy == 0 && Q.bruning_candidacy == 0) Q.stegerwald_candidacy = 1;
    }
    if (Q.bourgeois_votes < 35 && Q.cvp_left < 0) Q.vorbeck_candidacy = 1;
    if (Q.dnvp_left >= 0 && Q.bourgeois_votes >= 35) Q.westarp_candidacy = 1;
    if (Q.adenauer_candidacy == 0 && Q.bruning_candidacy == 0 && Q.stegerwald_candidacy == 0 && Q.vorbeck_candidacy == 0 && Q.westarp_candidacy == 0) Q.vorbeck_candidacy = 1;
    if (Q.westarp_candidacy && Q.vorbeck_candidacy) Q.westarp_candidacy = 0;

    if (Q.vorbeck_candidacy && Q.cvp_formed) {
        Q.westarp_candidacy = 0;
        Q.adenauer_candidacy = 0;
        Q.bruning_candidacy = 0;
        Q.stegerwald_candidacy = 0;
    }

    if (Q.adenauer_candidacy) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.second_reactionary_candidate = "Adenauer";
        if (!Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.reactionary_candidate = "Adenauer";
    }
    if (Q.bruning_candidacy) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.second_reactionary_candidate = "Brüning";
        if (!Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.reactionary_candidate = "Brüning";
    }
    if (Q.stegerwald_candidacy) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.second_reactionary_candidate = "Stegerwald";
        if (!Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.reactionary_candidate = "Stegerwald";
    }
    if (Q.westarp_candidacy) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.second_reactionary_candidate = "Westarp";
        if (!Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.reactionary_candidate = "Westarp";
    }
    if (Q.vorbeck_candidacy) {
        if (Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.second_reactionary_candidate = "Vorbeck";
        if (!Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.reactionary_candidate = "Vorbeck";
    }

    if (!Q.spd_campaign && Q.reactionary_candidate != "Westarp") Q.spd_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    if (!Q.spd_campaign) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    if (!Q.spd_campaign) Q.csrp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    if (Q.z_candidate != "Braun") Q.z_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.dbp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.bvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.csvd_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.cnblp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.wp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.kvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    if (Q.dnvp_left >= 0) Q.dnvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    Q.other_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;

    if (Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Adenauer" || Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Brüning" || Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Stegerwald") {
        if (!Q.spd_campaign) Q.spd_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        if (!Q.spd_campaign) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.dbp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        if (!Q.spd_campaign) Q.csrp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.z_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.bvp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.csvd_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
    } else if (Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Vorbeck" || Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Westarp") {
        Q.csvd_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.cnblp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.wp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.kvp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        if (Q.dnvp_left >= 0) Q.dnvp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
        Q.other_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
    }

    if (Q.reactionary_candidate == "Westarp" && !Q.second_reactionary_candidate) {
        Q.spd_campaign = 1;
        Q.spd_candidate = "Braun";
        Q.ddp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        Q.csrp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
    }
}
!}
priority: 1
max-visits: 1
go-to: candidate_selection

= Presidential Election Candidates

With the 1932 German Presidential election coming up next month, we need to decide whether to run a candidate of our own. [? if hindenburg_run: Though many are calling for us to support the incumbent Hindenburg, he is a symbol of german tradition and patriotism who, despite the turbulent recent years, has yet to outright dismantle the republican order. ?][? if hindenburg_run == 0: with Hindenburg retiring, the German Right was thrown off-balance and will have to decide upon a candidate soon. ?]

If we were to run our own candidate, our party has narrowed the choice down to two nominees: Karl Jarres, our candidate for the 1925 presidential election, supported by the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span> and the <span style="color: #B8996F;">**WP**</span>, who received a plurality during the first round. He is supported by our industrialist and nationalist elements, but the liberals aren't entirely opposed to him either, perhaps we can unite the German Right once more? From our left-wing, Hans Luther has become the most popular name, with an impressive portfolio as former Chancellor and Reichsbank President, we can expect him to garner much political support.

[? if hindenburg_run == 0: Finally, we could invite Hugo Eckener as a moderate candidate, a nationalist anti-<span style="color: #954B00;">**nazi**</span> Zeppelin pilot. ?]

Anyhow, let's see who will be the candidates on the campaign trail.

@candidate_selection


- @view_candidates_1: View the running candidates.

@view_candidates_1


- @hindenburg: Hindenburg is, of course, running once more.
- @reactionary_candidates: Who will be the successor to Hindenburg?

@hindenburg
face-image: img/portraits/Hindenburg.jpg
view-if: hindenburg_run

President Hindenburg is, of course, running for re-election, and many in our party are prepared to support him as the [? if dvp_left >= 0: last bastion of democracy against Hitler and the Nazis ?][? if dvp_left < 0: symbol of German nationalism and patriotism ?]. The Hindenburg Mythos serves as a powerful rallying point for all parties, as he maintains high personal popularity despite everything Germany has endured. However, the more support he receives from the German left and center, the more Hindenburg views it as a stain on his personal honor. The refusal of August von Mackensen and other high-ranking officers with whom he served during the war to embrace his candidacy proved particularly painful to the Reich president.

- @harzburg: We await the decision of the Harzburg Front.

@reactionary_candidates
view-if: hindenburg_run == 0

- @adenauer
- @bruning
- @stegerwald
- @vorbeck
- @westarp

@adenauer
title: Konrad Adenauer, the <span style="color: var(--z-color);">**[+ z_name +]**</span> candidate.
face-image: img/portraits/AdenauerKonrad.jpg
view-if: adenauer_candidacy
max-visits: 1
go-to: reactionary_candidates if second_reactionary_candidate != 0

Mayor of Cologne since the Republic's founding and aligned with Stegerwald's policies, he too is a staunch supporter of an interconfessional party, expanding its electorate to Protestant voters.

With local elections fast approaching, many parties have opted not to field their own candidates, instead consolidating their support behind a select few.

- @harzburg: We await the decision of the Harzburg Front.

@bruning
title: Heinrich Brüning, the <span style="color: var(--z-color);">**[+ z_name +]**</span> candidate.
face-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg
view-if: bruning_candidacy
max-visits: 1
go-to: reactionary_candidates if second_reactionary_candidate != 0

A man we are all too familiar with, leader of the party's parliamentary group, he is now running for hte most powerful position in Germany. Despite Brüning's known commitment towards austerity, he is a flexible and intelligent figure, who's unlikely to even humor the <span style="color: #954B00;">**nazis**</span> in government.

With local elections fast approaching, many parties have opted not to field their own candidates, instead consolidating their support behind a select few.

- @harzburg: We await the decision of the Harzburg Front.

@stegerwald
title: Adam Stegerwald, the <span style="color: var(--z-color);">**[+ z_name +]**</span> candidate.
face-image: img/portraits/StegerwaldAdam.jpg
view-if: stegerwald_candidacy
max-visits: 1
go-to: reactionary_candidates if second_reactionary_candidate != 0

Despite his background as a unionist, he is situated firmly on the party's right and one of the most vocal proponents for the formation of an interconfessional party, or in his words, a Christian, democratic, German, and social party.

With local elections fast approaching, many parties have opted not to field their own candidates, instead consolidating their support behind a select few.

- @harzburg: We await the decision of the Harzburg Front.

@vorbeck
title: Paul von Lettow-Vorbeck, an <span style="color: #808080;">**independent**</span>.
face-image: img/portraits/LettowVorbeckPaul.jpg
view-if: vorbeck_candidacy
max-visits: 1
go-to: reactionary_candidates if second_reactionary_candidate != 0

Somehow, the German Right has done it again, prompted by the decreasing vote share of the bourgeois parties, another famous commander from the Great War was convinced to run for public office. However, the path for the *Lion of Africa* will be much harder than it was for Hindenburg, the Right is divided, and threatened by a rising <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span>.

With local elections fast approaching, many parties have opted not to field their own candidates, instead consolidating their support behind a select few.

- @harzburg: We await the decision of the Harzburg Front.

@westarp
title: Count Kuno von Westarp, the [? if dnvp_left >= 0: <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed: <span style="color: #455B95;">**KVP**</span> ?] candidate.
face-image: img/portraits/WestarpKuno.jpg
view-if: westarp_candidacy
max-visits: 1
go-to: reactionary_candidates if second_reactionary_candidate != 0

The longtime patriarch of the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span>, while a moderate within the party, and even somewhat receptive of participation within the *Weimar* system, his goal remains the restoraion of the Kaiserreich.

With local elections fast approaching, many parties have opted not to field their own candidates, instead consolidating their support behind a select few.

- @harzburg: We await the decision of the Harzburg Front.

@harzburg
go-to: duesterberg

@duesterberg
face-image: img/portraits/DuesterbergTheodor.jpg

The Harzburg Front has split, with the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span> preferring to nominate their own candidate. After a deal between Hugenberg and the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**Stahlhelm**</span>, the Harzburg Front has nominated the deputy leader of their paramilitary, Theodor Duesterberg.

- @nsdap_selection: Who will the NSDAP run?


@nsdap_selection
go-to: hitler if not hitler_deported; goring if hitler_deported

@hitler

The Nazis will run Hitler. A victory for Hitler would mean the end of parliamentary democracy, and the beginning of an era of unspeakable horrors.

- @communist: We await the decision of the Communists.

@goring

Since Hitler has been deported, the Nazis will run Hermann Göring in his stead. He is widely seen as a proxy for Hitler, who, despite his legal persecution, retains a popular base who wishes to see him returned to Germany. A victory for him would mean the end of parliamentary democracy, and the beginning of an era of unspeakable horrors.

- @communist: We await the decision of the Communists.


@communist
face-image: img/portraits/ThälmannErnst.jpg

The <span style="color: var(--kpd-color);">**KPD**</span> will run Ernst Thälmann, their leader and candidate in 1925. He retains the support of the Soviet Union and broadly rejects constructive participation within the Republic.

- @socialist: We await the decision of the SPD.


@socialist
go-to: braun if spd_candidate == "Braun"; rosenfeld if spd_candidate == "Rosenfeld"; reactionary_spd if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate or spd_candidate = second_reactionary_candidate

@braun
face-image: img/portraits/BraunOtto.jpg

The <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**[+ spd_name +]**</span> will run Otto Braun, [? if prussia_leader != "Braun": former ?] Prussian Minister-President and candidate in the 1925 election. [? if ddp_exist and z_candidate != "Braun": The <span style="color: var(--ddp-color);">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is expected to support him. ?][? if z_candidate = "Braun": The <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**Social Democrats**</span> have managed to rally the *Weimar* parties for a second 1925. ?]

- @dvp: So, what is our decision? Should we run our own candidate, or support [+ reactionary_candidate +]?

@rosenfeld
face-image: img/portraits/RosenfeldKurt.jpg

The <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**[+ spd_name +]**</span> will run Kurt Rosenfeld, a minor figure from their Left faction. [? if ddp_exist: The <span style="color: var(--ddp-color);">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> is expected to support him. ?]

- @dvp: So, what is our decision? Should we run our own candidate, or support [+ reactionary_candidate +]?

@reactionary_spd

Alarmed by the current state of the Republic, the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**[+ spd_name +]**</span> has chosen not to run a candidate, and instead to support a bourgeoisie nominee, in hopes that they might not detroy democracy.

- @dvp: So, what is our decision? Should we run our own candidate, or support [+ reactionary_candidate +]?


@dvp

So, what's our choice?

- @support_reactionary: Support [+ reactionary_candidate +].
- @support_second_reactionary: Support [+ second_reactionary_candidate +].
- @run_eckener: Run Hugo Eckener as a unity candidate.
- @run_jarres: Run Karl Jarres as our candidate.
- @run_luther: Run Hans Luther as our candidate.
- @support_braun: Support Braun.

@support_reactionary
subtitle: This is the default option.
on-arrival: progressive_dissent += 10 if spd_campaign; dvp_candidate = reactionary_candidate

We will support [+ reactionary_candidate +] in this election.

- @endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements.

@support_second_reactionary
subtitle: This is the default option.
view-if: second_reactionary_candidate != 0
on-arrival: progressive_dissent += 10 if spd_campaign; dvp_candidate = second_reactionary_candidate

We will support [+ second_reactionary_candidate +] in this election.

- @endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements.

@run_eckener
choose-if: dvp_left >= 0 and resources >= 1
view-if: reactionary_candidate != "Hindenburg"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dvp_left < 0: Why would we run a republican candidate? ?][? if resources < 1: Not enough resources. (Need 1) ?]
subtitle: -1 resource - After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
on-departure: resources -= 1; nationalist_dissent += 10; dvp_campaign = 1; dvp_candidate = "Eckener";

We will run Hugo Eckener.

- @endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements.

@run_jarres
choose-if: dvp_left < 0 and resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dvp_left >= 0: The party prefers running Luther. ?][? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. (Need 2) ?]
subtitle: -2 resources - After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
on-departure: resources -= 2; labor_dissent += 5; industrialist_strength += 10; nationalist_strength += 5; dvp_campaign = 1; dvp_candidate = "Jarres";

We will run Karl Jarres.

- @endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements.

@run_luther
choose-if: dvp_left >= 0 and resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dvp_left < 0: The party prefers running Jarres. ?][? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. (Need 2) ?]
subtitle: -2 resources - After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
on-departure: resources -= 2; liberal_strength += 5; nationalist_dissent += 10; dvp_campaign = 1; dvp_candidate = "Luther";

We will run Hans Luther.

- @endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements.

@support_braun
subtitle: This is the default option.
view-if: spd_candidate == "Braun"
on-arrival: progressive_strength += 10; industrialist_dissent += 15; nationalist_dissent += 30; dvp_candidate = "Braun"

We will support Braun in this election.

- @endorsements: Scout out potential endorsements.

@endorsements

We can try to convince parties supporting other candidates to switch their support to [+ dvp_candidate +].

- @convince_spd: Convince the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**[+ spd_name +]**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_ddp: Convince the <span style="color: var(--ddp-color);">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_dbp: Convince the <span style="color: #38C538;">**DBP**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_csrp: Convince the <span style="color: #FF6B21;">**CSRP**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_z: Convince the <span style="color: var(--z-color);">**[+ z_name +]**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_csvd: Convince the <span style="color: #8ED8E4;">**CSVD**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_wp: Convince the <span style="color: #B8996F;">**WP**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_cnblp: Convince the <span style="color: #7FCEB1;">**CNBLP**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_kvp: Convince the <span style="color: #455B95;">**KVP**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @convince_dnvp: Convince the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span> to back [+ dvp_candidate +].
- @view_candidates: View party endorsements.
- @hope: We have concluded negotiations with other parties.

@convince_spd
view-if: dvp_candidate != "Westarp" and spd_candidate != dvp_candidate and spd_candidate != "Rosenfeld"
choose-if: spd_votes < (antidem_votes - kpd_votes) and (dvp_candidate == "Luther" or dvp_candidate == "Eckener")
unavailable-subtitle: The Social Democrats are stronger than the far-right. [? if dvp_candidate == "Jarres": They are not satisfied with our candidate choice. ?] 
go-to: convince_spd_success if (dvp_left >= 0 and spd_relation >= 50); convince_spd_fail if (dvp_left < 0 or spd_relation < 50)
max-visits: 1

We remind the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**[+ spd_name +]**</span> leaders that, in these exceptional times, splitting the democratic vote could have disastrous consequences.

@convince_spd_success
on-arrival: spd_relation += 3; spd_candidate = dvp_candidate; ddp_candidate = dvp_candidate if spd_campaign; csrp_candidate = dvp_candidate if spd_campaign; z_candidate = dvp_candidate if z_candidate == "Braun"; spd_campaign = 0;
go-to: endorsements

The SPD is convinced! They will be part of the [+ reactionary_candidate +] coalition.

@convince_spd_fail
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements

Unfortunately, we fail to turn the SPD away from [+ spd_candidate +]. 


@convince_ddp
view-if: ddp_exist and ddp_candidate != dvp_candidate
go-to: convince_ddp_success if ddp_relation >= 40; convince_ddp_fail if ddp_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

The liberal vote has been falling over time, especially during the current economic depression, so they will probably be of minimal help to us. Still, every little bit counts.

@convince_ddp_success
on-arrival: ddp_relation += 5; ddp_candidate = dvp_candidate
go-to: endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations and connections with their business wing, the [+ ddp_name +] is now campaigning for [+ reactionary_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_ddp_fail
on-arrival: ddp_relation -= 5
go-to: endorsements

Unfortunately, under the influence of their left wing, the [+ ddp_name +] has refused to support [+ reactionary_candidate +] for the presidency. 


@convince_dbp
view-if: dbp_exist and dbp_candidate != dvp_candidate
go-to: convince_dbp_success if dbp_relation >= 40; convince_dbp_fail if dbp_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the DBP to support [+ dvp_candidate +].

@convince_dbp_success
on-arrival: dbp_relation += 3; dbp_candidate = dvp_candidate
go-to: endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations, the DBP is now campaigning for [+ dvp_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_dbp_fail
on-arrival: dbp_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements

Unfortunately, the DBP has refused to support [+ dvp_candidate +] for the presidency.


@convince_csrp
view-if: csrp_exist and csrp_candidate != dvp_candidate
go-to: convince_csrp_success if csrp_relation >= 40; convince_csrp_fail if csrp_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the CSRP to support [+ dvp_candidate +].

@convince_csrp_success
on-arrival: csrp_relation += 3; csrp_candidate = dvp_candidate
go-to: endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations, the CSRP is now campaigning for [+ dvp_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_csrp_fail
on-arrival: csrp_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements

Unfortunately, the CSRP has refused to support [+ dvp_candidate +] for the presidency.


@convince_z
view-if: z_candidate != dvp_candidate and (cvp_formed == 0 or dvp_candidate != "Braun")
go-to: convince_z_success if z_relation >= 40; convince_z_fail if z_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the [+ z_name +] to support [+ dvp_candidate +].

@convince_z_success
on-arrival: {! 
    Q.z_relation += 3;
    Q.z_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
    if (Q.reactionary_candidate == "Adenauer" || Q.reactionary_candidate == "Brüning" || Q.reactionary_candidate == "Stegerwald") {
        if (!Q.second_reactionary_candidate){
            if (Q.spd_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.spd_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.ddp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate
            if (Q.dbp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.csrp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.csrp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.bvp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.bvp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.csvd_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.csvd_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.cnblp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.cnblp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.wp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.wp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.kvp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.kvp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.dnvp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.dnvp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.other_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.other_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            Q.reactionary_candidate = 0;
        } else {
            if (Q.spd_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.spd_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.ddp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate
            if (Q.dbp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.csrp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.csrp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.bvp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.bvp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
            if (Q.csvd_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.csvd_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            if (Q.cnblp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.cnblp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            if (Q.wp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.wp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            if (Q.kvp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.kvp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            if (Q.dnvp_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.dnvp_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            if (Q.other_candidate == Q.reactionary_candidate) Q.other_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            Q.reactionary_candidate = Q.second_reactionary_candidate;
            Q.second_reactionary_candidate = 0;
        }
    } else if (Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Adenauer" || Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Brüning" || Q.second_reactionary_candidate == "Stegerwald") {
        if (Q.spd_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.spd_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
        if (Q.ddp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate
        if (Q.dbp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.ddp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
        if (Q.csrp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.csrp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
        if (Q.bvp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.bvp_candidate = Q.dvp_candidate;
        if (Q.csvd_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.csvd_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        if (Q.cnblp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.cnblp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        if (Q.wp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.wp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        if (Q.kvp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.kvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        if (Q.dnvp_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.dnvp_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        if (Q.other_candidate == Q.second_reactionary_candidate) Q.other_candidate = Q.reactionary_candidate;
        Q.second_reactionary_candidate = 0;
    }
!}
go-to: endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations and connections with their right wing, the [+ z_name +] is now campaigning for [+ dvp_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_z_fail
on-arrival: z_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements

Unfortunately, the [+ z_name +] has refused to support [+ dvp_candidate +] for the presidency.


@convince_csvd
view-if: csvd_exist and csvd_candidate != dvp_candidate and dvp_candidate != "Braun"
go-to: convince_csvd_success if csvd_relation >= 40; convince_csvd_fail if csvd_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the CSVD to support [+ dvp_candidate +].

@convince_csvd_success
on-arrival: csvd_relation += 3; csvd_candidate = dvp_candidate
go-to: endorsements

Thanks to our friendly relations, the CSVD is now campaigning for [+ dvp_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_csvd_fail
on-arrival: csvd_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements

Unfortunately, the CSVD has refused to support [+ dvp_candidate +] for the presidency.


@convince_wp
view-if: wp_exist and wp_candidate != dvp_candidate and dvp_candidate != "Braun"
go-to: convince_wp_success if (wp_relation >= 40 and wp_radical == 0); convince_wp_fail if not (wp_relation >= 40 and wp_radical == 0)
max-visits: 1

